// THE ADVANCE RULES, WRITTEN ONCE. Finish calls this, Reroute calls it,
// and Edit Workflow should once its structure edits can move the active
// point. The flow will implement the same walk server side, and this is
// the version it mirrors.
//
// IT IS A FULL RECONCILE, NOT AN INCREMENT. Nothing here asks what just
// happened; it derives the whole state from the assignment rows as they
// now stand. That makes it idempotent, so running it twice is harmless,
// and it means a structure edit that inserts a phase before the current
// one is handled by the same code that handles a completion.
//
// PASS ONE marks every phase Completed or NotStarted purely from whether
// its REQUIRED assignments are all done. Optional assignments never hold
// up a phase, which is the whole point of the Required toggle. A phase
// with no assignments at all is NOT complete: an empty phase is a
// half-built workflow, not a finished one.
//
// PASS TWO finds the earliest phase that is not Completed, sets it
// InProgress, and starts the LOWEST assignment order in it that still
// has open work. Everyone sharing that order starts together, which is
// what parallel means here.
//
// ONLY NotStarted ROWS ARE STARTED. An assignment already InProgress
// keeps its StartDate and DueDate, so re-running this does not push
// someone's deadline out every time a colleague finishes something.
//
// NO PHASE LEFT means the request is Completed. The CompletedDate is
// cleared on the other branch, so a send-back reopening a finished
// request does not leave a completion date on a live request.
//
// WHAT THIS DELIBERATELY DOES NOT DO: touch a request that is OnHold,
// Suspended or Cancelled. Callers check that before calling. A reconcile
// that restarted a suspended request would defeat the suspension.

Patch(
    colAssignments,
    LookUp(colAssignments, AssignmentKey = locDetFinishKey),
